&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Why At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&amp;nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform – best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&amp;nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_InfoMsg iCIMS_InfoMsg_Job&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;iCIMS_Expandable_Text&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an SDET to join one of our agile engineering teams and help us build quality into LUMA, our scientific software platform. You&#39;ll take ownership of testing for a specific module of the application — writing and maintaining automated tests, exploring new features, and working alongside developers, application scientists and DevOps engineers to make sure what we ship is reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on automation role with room to grow. You&#39;ll be contributing to established test frameworks rather than building them from scratch, with support from senior SDETs who will help you develop your technical depth and your understanding of the science behind the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While the primary focus is automation, the role also involves manual exploratory testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;In this role you will get to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, maintain and extend automated test suites for your module using Cucumber, TypeScript and Cypress (and Playwright where we use it).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Own day-to-day quality for your area: contributing test scenarios during planning, testing stories as they&#39;re built, and giving the team a clear picture of release readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and document test cases that cover functional, regression and integration scenarios, and keep them useful as the product evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and reproduce defects, raise well-evidenced bug reports in JIRA, and verify fixes with developers and scientists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep your tests green and trustworthy in our CI pipelines, and help improve how tests run and report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn to read and interpret API documentation and turn it into meaningful automated coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leading experts in software development, scientific product management and test automation — and be mentored by them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have &lt;strong&gt;2–5 years&#39; experience in QA/testing, including at least a year of hands-on test automation&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;re comfortable working in a code-first way, you enjoy digging into how things work, and you&#39;re happy asking questions when a domain is unfamiliar. You work carefully and pay attention to detail, and you can take a story or module, understand it and devise a concrete approach to testing going above and beyond the standard acceptance criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Just as importantly, you want to get better. We&#39;re looking for someone who takes feedback well, is curious about the scientific problems our users are solving and wants to grow into a senior automation engineer over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Key Skills we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Practical experience with Cypress&lt;/strong&gt; — writing tests, using selectors and custom commands, debugging failures, and working within an existing Page Object Model. Experience testing React applications is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working knowledge of TypeScript or JavaScript&lt;/strong&gt;, including asynchronous code (promises, async/await). You don&#39;t need to be an expert in generics and interfaces, but you should be able to read and write clean, maintainable test code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with BDD / Cucumber&lt;/strong&gt;, or a willingness to pick it up quickly — we write most of our specs in Gherkin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test case design and documentation&lt;/strong&gt; — the ability to break a feature down into clear, repeatable scenarios and write them up so others can follow them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort with Git and GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;, including branching, pull requests and code review, plus experience working in JIRA or a similar tracking system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Playwright, or interest in learning it — we use it for a subset of our tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to API testing tools (Postman, REST clients) or writing API-level automated tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Any experience with performance or load testing (K6 or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Familiarity with validating data integrity across release upgrades, migrations or schema changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;A background or interest in science, engineering or research software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Research shows us the&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;confidence gap&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;imposter syndrome can get in the way of meeting outstanding candidates, so please don’t hesitate to apply — we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree that Dotmatics may collect your personal data for recruiting, global organization planning, and related purposes. Dotmatics &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.dotmatics.com/privacy-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; explains what personal information we may process, where we may process your personal information, our purposes for processing your personal information, and the rights you can exercise over Dotmatics use of your personal information.&lt;span class=&quot;c-message__edited_label&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dotmatics is an equal opportunity employer. We are a welcoming place for everyone, and we do our best to make sure all people feel supported and connected at work.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GoCardless is a global bank payment company. Over 100,000 businesses, from start-ups to household names, use GoCardless to collect, manage and send bank payments through Direct Debit, real-time payments and open banking. With US$130bn+ processed annually across 30+ countries, we handle recurring and one-off payments without the chasing, stress, or expensive fees. Our end-to-end payment platform also features AI-powered solutions to improve payment success and reduce fraud, alongside connections to over 350 platforms businesses use everyday.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are headquartered in the UK, with teams and operations spanning North America, Europe and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to hire an Emerging Account Executive to join our UK&amp;amp;I team. As an Emerging AE you will be responsible for finding and closing new business deals across the UK&amp;amp;I via your own efforts and supported by our marketing, partnerships and Sales Development teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be engaging with economic buyers within merchant accounts to identify and secure a role for GoCardless as a payment provider. You will liaise with a multitude of stakeholders and departments; from finance and engineering to marketing and procurement. By successfully multi-threading you will build business cases and ultimately secure commercial arrangements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve built a dynamic, collaborative culture in which we hire and develop smart, driven people that share our desire to do work we can be proud of.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What excites you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll love taking a data driven approach to pitching GoCardless as a payment provider to Emerging ($1-$30m) accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Closing multi-territory, multi-year deals with fast growing companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying high-fit accounts within your territory/ book of business&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing account plans, working with stakeholders in marketing to deliver those plans and building your network within those accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Selling the value of our global payments platform and then developing opportunities through negotiation to contract closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What excites us&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven sales experience in a B2B SaaS environment with a track record of achieving quota (total quota for this role is £500k per annum)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous sales experience in the Payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of working with some of our key verticals such as Utilities, Telco, Banking or Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to CxO (CFO/ CTO ideally) and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates with an understanding of the MEDDPICC Sales methodologies (or similar) and experience in applying them&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A structured sales approach, experience of using salesforce and prior experience of selling complex SaaS products and services (Selling APIs is not essential but a nice to have)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High activity: you are able to cover a large territory effectively and build a dynamic pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t expect you to meet every requirement. If you’re excited by this role, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base salary range:&lt;/strong&gt; £35,200 - £52,800 + OTE (100% of base)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary ranges are based on role, job level, location, and market data.&amp;nbsp; Please note that whilst we strive to offer competitive compensation, our approach is to pay between the &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;minimum and the mid-point&lt;/span&gt; (£35,200 - £44,000) of the pay range until performance can be assessed in role. Offers will take into account level of experience, interview assessment, budgets and parity between you and fellow employees at GoCardless doing similar work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(some of) The good stuff&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellbeing &lt;/strong&gt;- stay healthy with dedicated support and medical cover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work away scheme&lt;/strong&gt; - gives you the option to work away from your country of residence for up to 90 days in any 12 month period&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptive Working&lt;/strong&gt; - allows you to work flexibly, around your lifestyle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Parental leave&lt;/strong&gt; - to suit everyone embarking on life&#39;s great adventure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Budget&lt;/strong&gt; - lead your own development with an annual learning budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time off&lt;/strong&gt; - generous holiday allowance, + 3 annual volunteer days, + 4 annual business-wide wellness days (‘GC Fridays’)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at GoCardless&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re an organisation defined by our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocardless.com/g/values-operating-principles/&quot;&gt;values&lt;/a&gt;; We &lt;em&gt;start with why &lt;/em&gt;before we begin any project, to ensure it’s aligned with our mission. We&lt;em&gt; act with integrity&lt;/em&gt;, always. We &lt;em&gt;care deeply&lt;/em&gt; about what we do and we know it&#39;s essential that we &lt;em&gt;be humble &lt;/em&gt;whilst we do it. Working this way creates the GC magic- the reason we all love showing up to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
